   "source": [
    "## Tokenization"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "id": "0453d3dc-0ca6-45ce-85a7-1e9b168734c7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "for t5, we are using t5-tokenizer ....it has ~32k vocabulary\n",
    "\n",
    "In artificial intelligence and machine learning, tokenization is the process of breaking raw text down into smaller, manageable units—called tokens—so a model can read and process language.\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "options for tokenization-\n",
    "--> padding\n",
    "--> max-length  (can be any no. i.e. multiple of two)\n",
    "--> truncate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "8cd0100c-1180-41a3-b160-4669912b45e5",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "tokenizer= T5Tokenizer.from_pretrained(\"t5-small\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 60,
   "id": "c196a9dc-36b2-4c40-bad0-ec95cf6c6896",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "##raw data--> tokenized inputs for fine-tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "def tokenize(data):\n",
    "    inputs= tokenizer(data['dialogue'], padding= 'max_length', max_length= 512, truncation= True)\n",
    "    targets= tokenizer(data['summary'], padding='max_length', max_length=200, truncation= True)\n",
    "\n",
    "    inputs[\"labels\"]= targets[\"input_ids\"]  ## summary token_ids are added to inputs as labels\n",
    "    return inputs\n",
    "    "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 21,
   "id": "5554086d-a5ee-466f-9fbf-4ff2f94759a7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "train_dataset= train_data.apply(tokenize, axis=1).tolist()\n",
    "val_dataset= val_data.apply(tokenize, axis=1).tolist()"
   ]
